// Ch8 B01 "Landfall under the kites" (act1_ch08.md §2 B01; W01 → W02). In-engine, played on arrival.
// 10:40, warm noon (`ch08_day`). W01: the trader from Tamsule comes in under the seawall: grey laterite
// in a long curve, row upon row of Watchers (carved faces, eyes shut, mouths open as if humming), and
// dozens of cloth kites over the wall-head, flown because a Cantor has come, "so the Watchers have
// something to look up at". Act I's last festival frame. W02: on the mole steps a few townsfolk have
// come down to see the Cantor. Asha smiles first.
// Kerrid peels off: "Later." and he walks away along the outer foot of the wall, the way he declines
// inns. A plain exit, played as habit, with NO look back at the wall (rule 3: nothing stages Corrow as
// his return). Toma: "He does that." Nobody follows. The chapter flow drops him from the party after
// this scene; he is gone until B15.
title: ch08_landfall
location: ch08/corrow
---
@camera W01
@music corrow_day fade=2.0
@sfx gulls_far
@wait 3.0
@camera W02
@mark townsfolk_a mole_greet_a walk via=way_mole_parapet
@mark townsfolk_b mole_greet_b walk via=way_mole_parapet
@face asha smile 0.4
Townsfolk [smile]: The Cantor! Look up, look, they've put every kite out for you. #line:ch08_landfall_001
Asha [smile]: They're beautiful. Thank you. Are they all for the Watchers? #line:ch08_landfall_002
Townsfolk [soft_smile]: So they've got something to look up at, Lady. Their eyes are shut all year. #line:ch08_landfall_003
@mark asha day_asha walk via=way_mole_parapet,wall_foot
@mark toma day_toma walk via=way_mole_parapet,wall_foot
@wait 0.8
Kerrid [neutral]: Later. #line:ch08_landfall_004
@mark kerrid wall_foot walk via=way_mole_parapet
@wait 1.5
Rhen [neutral]: Where's he— #line:ch08_landfall_005
Toma [neutral]: He does that. #line:ch08_landfall_006
@wait 4.0
===
